Project 1: Simple Question and Answer ( simple LLM invoke)
from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI
llm = ChatOpenAI(model="gpt-4o-mini", api_key="YOUR_API_KEY")
resp = llm.invoke("Hello, how are you?")
print(resp.content)

from langchain_huggingface import HuggingFaceEndpoint
llm = HuggingFaceEndpoint(repo_id="facebook/blenderbot-400M-distill", huggingfacehub_api_token="YOUR_API_KEY")
resp = llm.invoke("Hello, how are you?")
print(resp)

Above code can be easily converted to app, by moving input and output to variables and read-write I/O

Chat Models (like ChatOpenAI) → expect structured messages (HumanMessage, AIMessage, etc.) and are designed for multi-turn dialogue.
Simple Question-Answer Models (like OpenAI or HuggingFaceEndpoint used as LLM) → expect plain text input and return plain text output, good for one-shot Q&A.
